✅2.5 Can we use the same Runnable object with multiple threads?
Yes.

Example:
Runnable task = new MyRunnable();

Thread t1 = new Thread(task);
Thread t2 = new Thread(task);

t1.start();
t2.start();

Output:

Thread-0 : Executing Runnable task
Thread-1 : Executing Runnable task

Why?
🔴 Runnable only contains the task.
🔴 It does not represent a thread.
🔴 Therefore, multiple threads can execute the same Runnable object.

Multiple threads can execute the same task.
Flow:

     Runnable Object
            |
    -----------------
    |               |
    ↓               ↓
Thread-1        Thread-2